<title>USA: Detroit Diesel in engine supply agreement.</title>
<headline>Detroit Diesel in engine supply agreement.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detroit Diesel Corp said Tuesday its Series 60 engine was now available in the new Van Hool T2100 Series of highway coaches and motorhomes made by ABC Bus Inc in North America.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the engine supply agreement were not announced.</p>
<p>Detroit Diesel said the Series 60 engine was rated for up to 500 horsepower.</p>
<p>The company makes a complete line of diesel engines for use in truck, fire and emergency vehicles, coaches and buses, and in industrial, military and civilian markets.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
